window.KB_BODY[61]={"tsb102311":"<h2>Revision, Symptom Tree t104, Lubricating Oil Pressure High, and Symptom Tree t105, Lubricating Oil Pressure Low</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a revision, Symptom Tree t104, Lubricating Oil Pressure High, and Symptom Tree t105, Lubricating Oil Pressure Low</p>","tsb102325":"<h2>Revision, Measure Step, Cylinder Block Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the main bearing bore diameter dimensions in the Measure Step of Procedure 001-026, Cylinder Block.</p>","tsb102339":"<h2>Revision, Initial Check Step, Injector Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 006-026 (Injector) in Section 6 of the Service Manual, QSK45 and QSK60, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The procedure is being revised to add information on how to determine if the high-pressure injection (HPI) injectors have run dry (without fuel) and to check the engine.</p>","tsb102346":"<h2>Revision, Assembly Step, Cylinder Head Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announcs a new drop gauge, Part Number 4918779. The drop gauge is used to measure valve guide straightness and diameter after pressing the valve guide into the cylinder head during cylinder head rebuild on the QSK45 and QSK60 engines.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102347":"<h2>Addition, Service Tool Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the Drop Gauge service tool for checking the valve guides, to the Service Tool Procedure 022-001_02 in Section 22.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102350":"<h2>Revision, Guided Step 2D, Fault Code 388</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Guided Step 2D specification for Fault Code 388 in the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Electronic Control System, Signature, ISX, and QSX15, Bulletin 3666259.</p>","tsb102366":"<h2>Revision, Troubleshooting Overview Procedure and Coolant Loss Symptom Tree</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Troubleshooting Overview Procedure t00-004 in Section TS and the Coolant Loss symptom tree.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102367":"<h2>Addition, Pressure Test Step, Cooling System Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the Pressure Test step to the Cooling System Procedure 008-018 in Section 8.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102368":"<h2>Addition, Service Tool Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds service tools Fluorescent Tracer Dye and Black Light Lamp Kit to the Service Tools Procedure 022-001_08 in Section 8.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102373":"<h2>Revision, Leak Test Step, Cylinder Head Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head) to include the test kit, Part Number 3164943, used to test the fuel passages in the Leak Test step of the procedure.</p>","tsb102381":"<h2>Revision, Shop Talk Section, Fault Code 187</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Shop Talk section of Fault Code 187 to add an explanation of fault code status so that proper troubleshooting is performed while the fault code is active.</p>","tsb102387":"<h2>Addition, Multiple Steps, Crankshaft Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the QSKV counter weight torque to the Clean and Inspect for Reuse step in the Crankshaft Procedure 001-016 in Section 1.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102388":"<h2>Revision, Install Step, Idler Gear, Camshaft (Right Bank) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to correct the positioning of the oil hole when assembling the right bank camshaft idler shaft on the QSK45 and QSK60 engine, <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-038-tr\">Procedure 001-038 (Idler Gear, Camshaft (Right Bank)) in Section 1.</a></p>","tsb102390":"<h2>Addition, Guided Steps 1C and 1C-1, Fault Code 433</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds Steps 1C and 1C-1 in Fault Code 433 in the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Electronic Control System, Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 3666259, to include voltage checks at the sensor and at the ECM to determine if low voltage from the ECM or high resistance in the harness is the cause of a fault.</p>","tsb102400":"<h2>Revision, General Information, Overhead Set (OBC) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic intends to make it clear that QSK45 and QSK60 engines with the Quantum fuel system (mechanically actuated injectors) no longer require a valve and injector set to be performed at 1500 hours. Instead, the valves and injectors will <b>only</b> be adjusted when the injector is serviced.</p><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the General Information step of Procedure 003-006 (Overhead Set (OBC)) to include a statement that reflects the guidelines for adjusting the overhead.</p>","tsb102401":"<h2>Revision, Maintenance Schedule</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic intends to make it clear that QSK45 and QSK60 engines with the Quantum fuel system (mechanically actuated injectors) no longer require a valve and injector set to be performed at 1500 hours. Instead, the valves and injectors will <b>only</b> be adjusted when the injector is serviced.</p><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the maintenance schedule, Procedure 102-002 (Maintenance Schedule) to remove the scheduled item for adjusting the overhead.</p>","tsb102402":"<h2>Revision, Circuit Illustration, Fault Codes 394 and 395</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the circuit illustration for Fault Codes 394 and 395 to correct ECM pin numbers.</p>","tsb102438":"<h2>Revision, Measure Step, Cylinder Block Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service Parts Topic revises the part numbers shown in the Measure Step of Procedure 001-056, Cylinder Block.</p>","tsb102441":"<h2>Revision, Symptom Tree t105, Lubricating Oil Pressure Low</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises symptom tree T105 (Lubricating Oil Pressure Low) to include additional steps for the instant loss of lubricating engine oil. The additional steps provide a list of components that <b>must</b> be checked when this condition occurs.</p>","tsb102445":"<h2>Revision to Troubleshooting Trees t022, t023, t024, and t096</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the following troubleshooting trees for the QSK45 and QSK60 engines:</p><ul><li><a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>-t022 - Coolant Temperature Above Normal - Gradual Overheat</li><li><a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>-t023 - Coolant Temperature Above Normal - Sudden Overheat</li><li><a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>-t024 - Coolant Temperature Below Normal</li><li><a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>-t096 - Intake Manifold Air Temperature Above Specification.</li></ul><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102453":"<h2>Revision, Symptom Tree t027, Crankcase Gases (Blowby) Excessive</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises symptom tree t027, Crankcase Gases (Blowby) Excessive.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102457":"<h2>Revision, Symptom Tree t027, Crankcase Gases (Blowby) Excessive</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises symptom tree t027, Crankcase Gases (Blowby) Excessive.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102460":"<h2>Revision, Clean and Inspect for Reuse, Cylinder Liner Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to revise the Clean and Inspect for Reuse steps for Procedure 001-028 (Cylinder Liner).</p>","tsb102469":"<h2>Revision, Install Step (Gear Cover, Front) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises procedure 001-031, (Gear Cover, Front), for the Troubleshooting and Repair Manuals listed.</p><p>The revision is the increase in the torque specification for the 6C, C8.3. C8.3G, C Gas Plus and L Gas Plus gear housing front cover.</p><p>The 10 mm head capscrews pass through the gear cover and thread into the front gear housing. The 11 mm head capscrews pass through the gear cover and the front gear housing and thread into the cylinder block.</p>","tsb102471":"<h2>Replacement, Intake Manifold Pressure Procedure, C Series Troubleshooting and Repair Manual</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic replaces Procedure 010-057 (Intake Manifold Pressure) in the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, C Series Engines, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666003\">3666003</a>.</p>","tsb102484":"<h2>Revision, Inspect Step, Lubricating Oil Filter (Spin-On) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises 007-013 (Lubricating Oil Filter (Spin-On)) the Inspect step to include aftercooler fretting as a possible location for aluminum in the oil.</p>","tsb102488":"<h2>Step Addition, Symptom Tree t047 (Engine Noise Excessive) and Symptom Tree t048 (Engine Noise Excessive - Combustion Knocks)</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a step calling for the removal of the engine vibration damper, and for the engine to be operated in the RPM range where the noise or knock occurs, to symptom trees t047 and t048 in the Service Manual, Signature, ISX, and QSX15, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p>","tsb102500":"<h2>Addition, Single and Double Nut Configuration Rebuild Instructions, (Fan Hub, Belt Driven) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds single nut (406 mm [15.98 in] diameter hub) and double nut (450 mm [17.72 in] diameter hub) configuration rebuild instructions to Procedure 008-036 (Fan Hub, Belt Driven).</p>","tsb102504":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Steps, Fault Codes 297 and 298</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic corrects the OEM Pressure Switch circuit illustration and pin numbers for Fault Codes 297 and 298.</p>","tsb102506":"<h2>Revision, Measure Step, Cylinder Block and Liner Seats Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-027 (Cylinder Block and Liner Seats) in Section 1 of the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. Oversize liners have been included.</p>","tsb102510":"<h2>Complete Revision, Sensor Wiring Harness Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the content from Procedures 019-043 (Engine Wiring Harness) to 019-081 (Sensor Wiring Harness). In addition, wiring harness bracket and cover torques have been included. Procedure 019-043 (Engine Wiring Harness) is no longer included in the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, CENSE™ System, QSK45 and QSK60 Engine Series, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666410\">3666410</a>.</p>","tsb102513":"<h2>Revision, Install Step, Injector Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the torque value of the mechanically actuated injector hold-down capscrew in Procedure 006-026 (Injector). The new torque value for the injector hold-down capscrew is 75 N•m [55 ft-lb].</p>","tsb102515":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Steps, Timing Pin Housing and Gear Housing (Front)</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic releases Procedure 001-049 (Timing Pin Housing) and revises Procedure 001-033 (Gear Housing, Front) to include a reference to Procedure 001-049 (Timing Pin Housing).</p>","tsb102530":"<h2>Revision, Preparatory Step, Engine Run-in (Without Dynamometer) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to revise the Preparatory Step for Procedure 014-004, Engine Run-in (Without Dynamometer). The requirements to pre heat the engine and the use of SAE 10W-30 lubricating oil has been removed.</p>","tsb102541":"<h2>Revision, Clean and Inspect for Reuse Step, Connecting Rod Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds information about supporting the connecting rod at the large bearing end to avoid I-beam damage in Procedure 001-014 (Connecting Rod) in Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p>","tsb102547":"<h2>Revision, Remove Step, Piston Cooling Nozzle Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to revise the Remove step in Procedure 001-046 (Piston Cooling Nozzle). This allows the field to reuse the piston cooling nozzles, providing they are handled with care and inspected before they are placed back into the engine.</p>","tsb102556":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Steps, Maintenance Schedule Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the maintenance schedule by removing the reference in the schedule to &#x27;see Section V for oil replacement based on analysis&#x27; statement and replacing the statement with a reference to the Cummins® Engine Oil and Oil Analysis Recommendations, Bulletin 3810340. Multiple revisions to the Oil Drain Interval step have been made also.</p>","tsb102557":"<h2>Revision, Assembly Step, Fan Drive Idler Arm Assembly Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is revise the assembly step in Procedure 008-029 (Fan Drive Idler Arm Assembly) in Group 8. The procedure now includes a slide arm design idler assembly.</p>","tsb102558":"<h2>Revision, Clean and Inspect for Reuse Steps, Lubricating Oil Cooler and Lubricating Oil Thermostat Procedures</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic identifies how to inspect the oil thermostat seat depth in the oil cooler housing in Procedure 007-003 (Lubricating Oil Cooler) and adds a link in Procedure 007-039 (Lubricating Oil Thermostat) in the Signature, ISX, QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p><p>Shallow thermostat seat depth can lead to damaged oil thermostats and problems with oil pressure fluctuation. If the seat depth dimension is below the minimum specification, the oil cooler housing will need to be replaced.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Distance From Seat to Spot Face at End of Lubricating Oil Cooler Housing</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>123.47 mm</td><td>Minimum Dimension</td><td>4.861 inch</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07c00546.png\" alt=\"07c00546.png\"></figure><p>Use this reference dimension for the following lubricating oil cooler housing part numbers: 4952496, 4952497, 4952507, and 4952508.</p>","tsb102561":"<h2>Revision, Inspect for Reuse Step, Camshaft Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises a note in the Clean and Inspect step in Procedure 001-008 (Camshaft). The note identifies additional components to replace if a new camshaft is installed.</p>","tsb102563":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Steps, (Crankshaft Seal, Front) and (Gear Cover, Lower) Procedures</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-023 (Crankshaft Seal, Front) and Procedure 001-080 (Gear Cover, Lower). Both procedures were updated to clarify the replacement of the lower gear covers with a beveled half groove or a full o-ring groove under the crankshaft seal flange.</p><p>The full o-ring groove covers, contain an o-ring in the lower gear cover groove and were only used prior to June 5, 1999. The lower gear cover <b>must</b> be replaced if installing a new seal.</p><p>The beveled half groove covers do <b>not</b> contain an o-ring and <b>only</b> require replacement if damaged.</p>","tsb102584":"<h2>Revision, Symptom Tree, Coolant in the Lubricating Oil</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises symptom tree t025 (Coolant in the Lubricating Oil) in Section TS, to check for coolant leaks in the EGR cooler.</p>","tsb102590":"<h2>Revision, Fuel System - Left Side View, Engine Diagrams Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the order in the list of components on the &#x27;Fuel System - Left Side View&#x27; for Procedure 100-002 (Engine Diagrams).</p>","tsb102603":"<h2>Revision, Specifications Section, Cooling System Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts topic is to revise Procedure 018-018 (Cooling System) in Section V of the Service Manual Signature, ISX, and QSX15, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. The specification for Maximum Coolant Pressure has been changed.</p>","tsb102613":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Steps, Fault Code 115, 121, and 433</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises multiple steps in the following fault codes:</p><p>Guided Step 2D to replace the ECM for active fault code 115 if no other faults are identified.</p><p>Guided Step 2D to replace the ECM for active fault code 121 if no other faults are identified.</p><p>Guided Step 4E to replace the ECM for active fault code 343 if no other faults are identified.</p>","tsb102618":"<h2>Revision, Torque Value, (Bearings, Main) and Crankshaft Procedures</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the torque specification for main bearing side bolts in Procedures 001-006 (Bearings, Main) and 001-016 (Crankshaft) in Section 1.</p>","tsb102624":"<h2>Revision, Fuel Flow Graphic, (Fuel System - Overview) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to revise the Aftertreatment Injector Fuel Flow diagram for automotive applications with CM871.</p>","tsb102625":"<h2>Revision, Maintenance Schedule</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic removes Procedure 003-018 (Crankcase Breather Tube) from Section 8 (Maintenance Procedures at 200,000 Kilometers [125,000 Miles], 3000 Hours, or 2 Years) of the Signature and ISX Operation and Maintenance Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666251\">3666251</a>. This procedure is already listed in Section 3 (Maintenance Procedures at Daily Interval). In addition, Procedure 102-002 (Maintenance Schedule) is revised accordingly in the Signature and ISX Operation and Maintenance Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666251\">3666251</a> and the ISX Engines Owners Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4960314\">4960314</a>.</p>","tsb102627":"<h2>Revision, Circuit Diagram, Fault Code 482</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Fault Code 482 to include a numbered component list to follow the system circuit graphic.</p>","tsb102632":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Steps, Camshaft Bushings Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-010 (Camshaft Bushings) in Section 1 to include camshaft bushing bore reuse specifications.</p>","tsb102642":"<h2>Revision, Adjust Step, Overhead Set Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the maintenance interval reference in the Adjust Step in Procedure 003-004 (Overhead Set).</p>","tsb102657":"<h2>Complete Replacement, Cylinder Block Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic releases common Procedure 001-026 (Cylinder Block) for the QSK45, QSK60, QSK45G, and QSK60G engines.</p>","tsb102666":"<h2>New Procedure, Piston and Cylinder Liner</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces new Procedure 001-045 (Piston and Cylinder Liner) to the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p><p>The procedure includes the removal and installation steps required for the new straight split connecting rod used in QSK45 and QSK60 engines. The cylinder liner, piston and connecting rod <b>must</b> be removed as a complete assembly.</p>","tsb102668":"<h2>Revision, Remove Step, Crankshaft Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Remove Step in Procedure 001-016 (Crankshaft) in Section 1, of the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The Main Bearing Cap Puller service tool number has been revised.</p>","tsb102696":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Steps, Turbocharger Wastegate Actuator Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic is revising Procedure 010-050 (Turbocharger Wastegate Actuator). The update is including the different adjustment procedures for the actuator end-link without a turnbuckle and actuator end-link with a turnbuckle.</p>","tsb102697":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Steps, Connecting Rod Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of the Service/Parts Topic is to add a General Information section, revise the Clean and Inspect for Reuse section, and revise the Measure section in the Connecting Rod procedure (001-014).</p>","tsb102706":"<h2>Revision, Troubleshooting Tree t021, Coolant Loss - Internal</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces an additional step in the Coolant Loss - Internal troubleshooting symptom tree for the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p><p>An incorrect or malfunctioning radiator cap can have an effect on the cooling system and cooling system components. The second step in the Coolant Loss - Internal symptom tree identifies a cause and correction relating to the radiator cap.</p>","tsb102719":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Sections, Piston Cooling Nozzle Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises multiple sections of Procedure 001-046 (Piston Cooling Nozzle). There are now two types of piston cooling nozzles available for QSK45 and QSK60 engines. This procedure has been updated to include information to distinguish between the two nozzle types.</p>","tsb102720":"<h2>Revision, Install Section, Crosshead Procedure and Revision, Clean and Inspect for Reuse Section, Cylinder Head Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts topic revises two procedures in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual:</p><p>002-001 (Crosshead) in Section 2, the Install section, valve stem tip check has been added.</p><p>002-004 (Cylinder Head) in Section 2, the Inspect for Reuse section, valve stem tip check has been added.</p>","tsb102726":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Sections, Engine Base Timing Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to revise the Adjust section of Procedure 001-088 (Engine Base Timing).</p>","tsb102728":"<h2>Release of (Gear Housing, Front) and Cylinder Block Liner Bore Concentricity Procedures</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic releases Procedure 84-001-033 (Gear Housing, Front) for the QSK45G and QSK60G engines and common Procedure 102-001-070 (Cylinder Block Liner Bore Concentricity) for the QSK45, QSK60, QSK45G, and QSK60G engines.</p>","tsb102736":"<h2>Revision, Crankshaft Wear Sleeve, Rear Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts topic revises the torque value for the rear seal carrier mounting bolts in Procedure 001-067 (Crankshaft Wear Sleeve, Rear) in Section 1. The revised torque reduces the likelihood of rear seal carrier oil leaks.</p><p>This change went into effect at Cummins Consolidated Diesel in July of 2003. The ESN first was 46773606. This change went into effect at Darlington in February of 2003. The ESN first was 21552187.</p>","tsb102744":"<h2>Revision, Specifications, Lubricating Oil System</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts topic revises the specifications for the Lubricating Oil System, sump configuration and capacities.</p>","tsb102759":"<h2>Addition, Service Tools Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces the addition of Loctite™ 518, Flexible Anerobic Gasket Sealant to Procedure 022-001 (Service Tools) in Section 1.</p>","tsb102761":"<h2>Revision, Inspect for Reuse Section, (Fan Hub, Belt Driven) and (Fan Spacer and Pulley) Procedures</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts topic introduces a change being made to the fan hub that is presently used on a variety of B/C/L applications. This change is to alter the dimension of the fan hub chamfer to increase the durability of the fan pulley. The change is to request that in the case of fan pulley damage, the technician also inspects the fan hub for damage to the chamfer and mating surface, and to replace. The fan hub if damage is found. It was decided to make this change requesting the inspection, because the change to the fan hub chamfer does <b>not</b> include a part number change.</p><p>The change in Procedure 008-039 (Fan Spacer and Pulley) instructs the technician to inspect the fan hub in Procedure 008-036 (Fan Hub, Belt Driven) of the appropriate manual.</p>","tsb102793":"<h2>Additional Step, Symptom Tree T021, Coolant Loss - Internal</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises symptom tree T021, Coolant Loss - Internal, by adding a check for a coolant leak on the turbocharger housing.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102795":"<h2>Addition, Fault Code 951</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces the addition of Fault Code 951 to the Signature™, ISX and QSX15 Electronic Control System T&amp;R Manual, Bulletin 3666259.</p>","tsb102796":"<h2>Revision, Clean and Inspect for Reuse Section, Crankshaft Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates the Clean and Inspect for Reuse section of Procedure 001-016 (Crankshaft) to state that if damage is found to the tone wheel, the tone wheel, <b>not</b> the crankshaft, <b>must</b> be replaced.</p>","tsb102801":"<h2>Revision, General Information, Procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head)</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a new stamping code that indicates the size of the valve guide seal for all K and QSK ReCon® cylinder heads. The stamping code was implemented on 5 February 2008.</p>","tsb102804":"<h2>Revision, General Information, Procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head)</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a new stamping code that indicates the size of the valve guide seal for all K and QSK ReCon® cylinder heads. The stamping code was implemented on 5 February 2008.</p>","tsb102836":"<h2>Engine Run-in (Without Dynamometer) Procedure, Preparatory Steps Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic supersedes 07T14-1. Replace 07T14-1 with this topic. Two notes were taken out of the Preparatory Step that no londer apply to the procedure.</p>","tsb102838":"<h2>Addition, Measure Step, Lubricating Oil Filter (Spin-On) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a Measure step to Procedure 007-013 (Lubricating Oil Filter (Spin-On)) in Section 7 of the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>, to check for a plugged filter by measuring the pressure drop across the lubricating oil filter.</p>","tsb102845":"<h2>Symptom Tree t122 (Turbocharger Leaks Engine Oil or Fuel) Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises symptom tree t122 (Turbocharger Leaks Engine Oil or Fuel). A check for turbocharger actuator cross shaft oil seal leakage was added to the end of the tree.</p>","tsb102846":"<h2>Service Tool Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 022-001 (Service Tools) for the Air Intake System with the addition of service tool, Part Number 4919166. This new service tool is used to remove and install the turbocharger actuator cross shaft bushing and oil seal on variable geometry turbochargers.</p>","tsb102851":"<h2>Addition, Measurement for Oversize Head Gasket for Cylinder Block and Liner Seats Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds measurement specifications for oversize head gaskets to the Clean and Inspect for Reuse step in Procedure 001-027 (Cylinder Block and Liner Seats).</p>","tsb102853":"<h2>Low-Temperature Aftercooler Water (LTA) Pump Procedure, Oil Feed Hose Information Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Remove and Install sections of Procedure 008-109 (Low-Temperature Aftercooler (LTA) Water Pump). Instructions for the oil feed hose has been included.</p>","tsb102854":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Pump Procedure, Clean and Inspect for Reuse Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Clean and Inspect for Reuse section of Procedure 007-031 (Lubricating Oil Pump). The pressure regulator spring specifications were revised.</p>","tsb102856":"<h2>(Crankshaft Seal, Rear) Procedure, Remove and Install Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-024 (Crankshaft Seal, Rear) to add information regarding the use of the rear crankshaft seal replacer kit, Part Number 3164780, and spacer, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4918688\">4918688</a>.</p>","tsb102869":"<h2>Injector Protrusion Procedure Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the conversion in Procedure 002-022 (Injector Protrusion).</p>","tsb102871":"<h2>Maintenance Schedule Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces crankcase breather element replacement to Section 6 of Procedure 102-002 (Maintenance Schedule).</p>","tsb102872":"<h2>Crankcase Breather (Internal) Procedure, Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces the addition of Procedure 003-002 (Crankcase Breather (Internal)) in Section 6 of the QSX15 Base Engine Operation and Maintenance Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666423\">3666423</a>.</p>","tsb102878":"<h2>Bearings, Connecting Rod and Piston and Connecting Rod Assembly Procedures Install Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Install section of Procedures 001-005 (Bearings, Connecting Rod) and 001-054 (Piston and Connecting Rod Assembly) in the K19 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021499\">4021499</a>.</p>","tsb102883":"<h2>Lubricating Oil System Specifications, Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces revisions to Procedure 018-017 (Lubricating Oil System) in the Specifications section.</p><ul><li>A specification has been added for the pressure drop across the lubricating oil filter.</li><li>A specification has been revised for the maximum oil pressure in cold conditions.</li></ul>","tsb102884":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Pan Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The Service/Parts Topic revises the Install section in Procedure 007-025 Lubricating Oil Pan in Section 7. A step has been added to loosen and tighten the mounting capscrew in the number one location.</p>","tsb102897":"<h2>(Fan Hub, Belt Driven) Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revised Procedure 008-036 (Fan Hub, Belt Driven) in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>, with the removal of the K38 and K50 manual sections from this procedure.</p>","tsb102902":"<h2>Crankshaft Seals, RTV on Outer Diameter</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic supercedes topic 06T1-28. Replace 06T1-28 with this topic.</p><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates Procedure 001-023 (Front Crankshaft Seal) and Procedure 001-024 (Rear Crankshaft Seal).</p><p>When the front or rear crankshaft seals are installed, it is necessary to apply a small bead of high performance RTV sealant Part Number 4918771 (Loctite™5920) or equivalent to the outside diameter of the seal. The purpose of the RTV is to reduce the possibility of oil leaks between the seal and the mounting plate. The engine serial number first with this seal configuration is 331157377, built 04 August 2004.</p><p>Crankshaft Seals requiring high performance RTV sealant Part Number 4918771 (Loctite™5920) or equivalent:</p><ul><li>Front crankshaft seal, Part Number 4100624</li><li>Rear crankshaft seal, Part Number 4100625</li></ul><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102921":"<h2>Camshaft Procedure, Remove Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a table, Camshaft Guide Installation Chart, to the Remove Section of the Camshaft procedure to show the correct c-clip positions for the camshaft removal tool.</p>","tsb102922":"<h2>New Lubricating Oil Filter Plugged Symptom Tree</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a Lubricating Oil Filter Plugged symptom tree to the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p>","tsb102924":"<h2>Troubleshooting Symptom Tree t105 Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates symptom tree t105 (Lubricating Oil Pressure Low). Multiple steps were updated to improve troubleshooting logic.</p>","tsb102926":"<h2>Troubleshooting Symptom Tree t105 Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates symptom tree t105 (Lubricating Oil Pressure Low). Multiple steps were updated to improve troubleshooting logic.</p>","tsb102931":"<h2>Revision, Cylinder Liner Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-028 (Cylinder Liner) in the K19 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021499\">4021499</a>. The Remove step has been revised to change the recommended cylinder liner removal service tool to Part Number 3163745.</p>","tsb102936":"<h2>Revision, Cylinder Liner Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-028 (Cylinder Liner) in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The Remove step has been revised to change the recommended cylinder liner removal service tool to Part Number 3163745.</p>","tsb102942":"<h2>Engine Base Timing Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-008 (Engine Base Timing) in Section 1 of the Service Manual, Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Engines, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. This Service/Parts Topic adds a step for cleaning the Loctite™ residue from the camshaft nose after the camshaft gear has been removed. Information has also been added for inspecting the camshaft gear for cracking around the puller holes. A new step was also added for applying Loctite™ 609, Part Number 3823718, to the inside diameter of the camshaft gear before the gear is installed.</p>","tsb102944":"<h2>Cooling System Procedure, Fill Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 008-018 (Cooling System) in Section 8 of the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, C Series Engines, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666003\">3666003</a> and Troublehsooting and Repair Manual, C8.3G, C Gas Plus, and L Gas Plus Engines, Bulletin 3666206. A caution and information related to the operation of the cab heater were added to the Fill section.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102948":"<h2>Additional Inspection Steps, Two Procedures and One Symptom Tree</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Troubleshooting Symptom Tree t105 (Lubricating Oil Pressure Low) in Section TS, Procedure 007-013 (Lubricating Oil Filter (Spin-On)) and Procedure 007-067 (Eliminator Filter) in Section 7 of the Service Manual, QSK45 and QSK60, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. A change was made to inspect the lubricating pump idler shaft and gear in the Inspect section if debris is found.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102977":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Pan Procedure, Note Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a note to explain that the C and L Series engines have several oil pan sealing options and to use the sealing method originally used for the oil pan.</p>","tsb102986":"<h2>Fleetguard™ Centrifuge Procedure, Assemble Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Assemble section in Procedure 007-068 (Fleetguard™ Centrifuge) to include a new illustration and additional instructions to be used in the assembly process.</p>","tsb102992":"<h2>Main Bearing Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic supersedes Service/Parts Topic 06T1-12. Replace Service/Parts Topic 06T1-12 with this Service/Parts Topic.</p><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-006 (Bearings, Main). The number of main bearing cap surfaces on each cap to apply a bead of Loctite™ 518 thread sealant has changed from four to two surfaces on each main bearing cap before installation into the cylinder block. This step will help seal and protect the surfaces between the main bearing cap and cylinder block. The relevant illustration has been revised to show the correct location to add the Loctite™ 518 thread sealant.</p>","tsb102996":"<h2>Service Tools Procedure, New Cylinder Block Protective Plugs</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds Protective Plug, Part Number 4918874 and Protective Plug, Part Number 4918875, to Procedure 022-001 (Service Tools) in Section 1 of the Signature™, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p><p>These new protective plugs are used in the front and rear oil passages of the cylinder block during repairs. The protective plugs protect the cylinder block from debris that can enter the oil passages. These protective plugs can <b>only</b> be used on cylinder blocks from engines built after August 2006. These new protective plugs were released because the oil passages were slightly modified and the available plugs no longer fit in the oil passages.</p>","tsb103000":"<h2>Camshaft Bushings Procedure, Remove Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Remove Section of Procedure 001-010 (Camshaft Bushings) in Section 1 of the C Series Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666003\">3666003</a>. The bushing installation and remove tool part number has changed and the Hydraulic Actuator Kit has been added along with the Camshaft Bushing Installation/Removal Kit.</p>"};
